We need implement. Need think architecture satisfying all. Need output-queued switch, 4x4, 2 frames per output max. Need parallel disjoint pairs >=2 beats/cycle at 4x4. Need no HOL across inputs, atomicity, forward progress, no m_valid combinational on m_ready. Need both tools.

We need design robust and synthesizable. Let's reason.

We have S inputs, M outputs. Frames up to 8 beats. Inputs have valid/ready. We can choose accept only when can buffer? Need per-output queues bounded 2 frames. Simplest: per-output FIFO of beats, but B1 at most 2 frames per output = 16 beats. If we buffer beats per output, need ensure frame atomicity and no interleaving. We can accept beats from inputs and push into per-output FIFO. But if multiple inputs target same output, need avoid interleaving frames. If we accept a frame's beats and push into FIFO, frame atomic if we don't interleave. But inputs may stall mid-frame; if output FIFO contains partial frame, another input cannot push to same output until frame complete. That's okay, but can cause HOL for that output only. Need no HOL across inputs: input blocked to busy output must not block different input to free output. Per-output independent FIFOs and arbiters can handle.

But B1: at most 2 frames per output. If we buffer beats, need track frames. Could implement per-output two frame buffers (store-and-forward) or per-output FIFO with frame count <=2. Need accept frames only if output has space for entire frame? Since frame length unknown until last, but max 8. We can allocate a frame slot per output when first beat accepted, then accept up to 8 beats. Need two slots per output. That's store-and-forward per frame: each output has 2 frame buffers, each up to 8 beats. Inputs arbitrate for a free frame slot at destination. Once a frame starts writing to slot, input streams its beats; output can drain completed frames. This gives atomicity, bounded 2 frames per output, parallel across outputs. But does it allow C1 >=2 beats/cycle? At 4x4 with all inputs backlogged to different outputs, each output can drain from its frame buffer. If store-and-forward, output can only start after entire frame received. But steady-state: each output has two buffers; one draining while another filling. Each output can deliver 1 beat/cycle if ready. With 4 outputs, aggregate up to 4 beats/cycle. But input side: each input sends to distinct output. Each input can fill its output's buffer. Need input accept rate. If each frame 8 beats, store-and-forward: output drains 8 beats, input fills next 8. Should sustain maybe 4 beats/cycle aggregate if each output drains continuously. But there is arbitration per output among inputs; at 4x4 disjoint, each output has one input, so no contention. Each output buffer can drain 1 beat/cycle. Inputs can fill at 1 beat/cycle. With two buffers, while one drains, other fills. Should work. Need ensure m_valid not depend on m_ready. Output valid from buffer non-empty. Good.

Alternative per-output FIFO with frame boundaries. Store-and-forward frame slots simpler. Need handle variable frame length up to 8. Need track write count and last. Need output read from completed frame. Need two slots per output: state free, writing, full, reading? Actually can have two frame buffers each with data array [0..7], keep, len, valid/full. Input writes into a free slot; when last beat accepted, mark full. Output selects a full slot and reads beats sequentially. Once last read, free slot. Since two slots per output, one can be writing while another full/reading. But if output is reading a full slot, another slot can be writing. If both slots full, no more input accepted to that output. That's B1: at most 2 frames per output. Good.

