Need handle multiple inputs targeting same output: write arbiter grants one input at a time to write a beat into a slot? Actually once a slot allocated to an input, that input owns it until frame complete. Other inputs cannot write to same slot. They can allocate other free slot if available. With 2 slots, at most 2 inputs can be writing/full per output. If both slots occupied (one writing, one full/reading), a third input to same output must wait. That's allowed. But could cause HOL? Only for that input; other inputs to other outputs proceed. C2: one output held not-ready and input backlogged to it; different input to ready output must deliver. Our per-input independent, yes. But if the blocked input's dest output has both slots occupied by other inputs? It waits, but doesn't block other input to ready output. Good.

