Need memory: per output 2 slots * 8 beats * DATA_W. For 4x4 32-bit: 4*2*8*32 = 2048 bits data plus keep. Fine. Need arrays in SystemVerilog. Use packed arrays or unpacked. For synthesis and both tools, use packed arrays with indices. E.g., logic [DATA_W-1:0] buf_data [M_COUNT][2][8]; logic [KEEP_W-1:0] buf_keep [M_COUNT][2][8]; logic [3:0] buf_len [M_COUNT][2]; logic buf_full [M_COUNT][2]; logic buf_busy? Actually need distinguish free vs writing vs full. We need know if slot is free for allocation. A slot can be free, writing (allocated but not full), or full. We can use state: 0 free, 1 writing, 2 full. Or use full flag and writing flag. Since at most one input writes a slot, we can track owner? But allocation grants slot to an input; input then writes beats. We need know slot is occupied (not free) until read complete. Use slot_state: 0 free, 1 writing, 2 full. When allocated, set to writing. On last beat, set to full. When output finishes reading last beat, set to free. Good. Need also track write beat count per slot? The input knows beat index? We can maintain per-input beat count for active frame. When writing a beat to slot, we need write address = input's beat count. Since input owns slot, can use per-input beat counter. Or per-slot write count. Per-input simpler: each input has active slot and beat_idx. On first beat, beat_idx=0. Write at beat_idx. If last, mark full and set len = beat_idx+1. Then input idle. Else beat_idx++. Need ensure max 8; harness guarantees. We can use 3-bit beat_idx (0..7). On last at beat_idx, len = beat_idx+1. Good.

